# Laravel Boost For PetConnect

Use Laravel Boost MCP tools when working on this Laravel 12 project.

- Use `search-docs` before making changes that depend on Laravel ecosystem APIs such as Laravel, Inertia, Fortify, Nova, Pest, Wayfinder, Tailwind, or Media Library.
- Use route/artisan/database tools when checking live route names, command options, or local data.
- Treat `.cursor/rules/00-petconnect-project.mdc` as the authoritative project context.
- Follow the more specific backend, frontend, and testing rules in this directory when their file globs apply.
- Do not use Boost docs for packages that are not installed here unless the user explicitly asks to add them.
